WEBVTT

00:05:59.185 --> 00:06:01.978
but not so much
that you entirely collapse, right?

00:06:02.327 --> 00:06:07.656
AG: I worry a little bit that calling,
kind of, everyday stress burnout,

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.906
it starts to medicalize the problem.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.463
And it reifies it in a way
that makes people feel like,

00:06:13.487 --> 00:06:16.876
"Oh, I have this horrible condition
and I can't function."

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:19.186
And then it becomes
a self-fulfilling prophecy,

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:21.169
as opposed to normalizing it and saying,

00:06:21.193 --> 00:06:23.629
"You know what? Everybody
has stress in their jobs.

00:06:23.653 --> 00:06:25.546
And that doesn't mean I'm burned out."

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.570
It just sounds a little ridiculous to say,

00:06:27.594 --> 00:06:31.526
"Oh, I'm overworked,
because I have to answer emails all day."